# Renders what the extension contributed to the TypoScript of this site, and nothing
# else. The constant is what "constants.typoscript" of the component assigns, the copied
# value is what its "setup.typoscript" assigns - so a delivery mechanism that did not
# reach this site renders an empty or a literal value here.
#
# The first constant is deliberately one that no "settings.definitions.yaml" declares: a
# site set contributes its settings as constants after the constants of its "typoscript"
# folder, so a declared path renders even when "constants.typoscript" was never read. The
# last two blocks render paths that both files declare, which is how their defaults are
# kept in step - they are the only values here that agree through either mechanism for
# that reason rather than by delivery. The switches of block 40 render the same
# characters both ways; the one of block 50 does not, because a site setting that is
# false reaches the constants as the empty string while the constant is assigned "0".
page = PAGE
page {
  10 = TEXT
  10.value = {$plugin.tx_academicstudyplan.view.templateRootPath}
  10.wrap = <div id="constant">|</div>

  20 = TEXT
  20.value < tt_content.academic_study_plan.templateName
  20.wrap = <div id="setup">|</div>

  30 = TEXT
  30.value < tt_content.academic_study_plan.partialRootPaths.100
  30.wrap = <div id="substituted">|</div>

  40 = TEXT
  40.value = {$plugin.tx_academicstudyplan.assets.css}|{$plugin.tx_academicstudyplan.assets.js}
  40.wrap = <div id="assets">|</div>

  50 = TEXT
  50.value = {$plugin.tx_academicstudyplan.filter.collapsible}
  50.wrap = <div id="collapsible">|</div>
}
